# Editor and interpreter debris
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# Hand-made backups. There were 63 of these at first import: APKBUILD.bak-r51,
# APKBUILD.before-dtb-second-*.bak and so on. They are what a repository exists
# to replace, so they are excluded rather than committed and then deleted.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.before-*.bak
# ...and the naming that slipped past those three: 26 kernel APKBUILD copies
# called APKBUILD.r170-before-r171, APKBUILD.before-r219,
# APKBUILD.r175-backup-20260810 and so on were committed, then deleted in r294,
# along with a patch parked as 0121-*.patch.staged.
APKBUILD.r[0-9]*
APKBUILD.before-*
APKBUILD.*-backup-*
*.staged

# Never commit, whatever a future .gitignore-less copy of this tree contains.
# Nothing matching these was present at first import; they are here so that a
# careless `git add -A` cannot introduce one later.
key.txt
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
*_rsa
*secret*
*token*
.env
.env.*

# Owner-imported stock firmware. These are proprietary Amazon files, extracted
# by each owner from their OWN device, and must never be redistributed:
#   coefs_FBF.cfg, coefs_FilterBank_640.cfg   Fire OS 5 chain
#   AFE.cfg, coefs_FBFV2_*, coefs_FilterBank_*  Fire OS 6 chain
#   vad_lite.tflite                           the stock DNN VAD
# The importer verifies them by hash at install time; the repository carries the
# contract, never the content.
vad_lite.tflite
AFE.cfg
coefs_*.cfg
# The speaker correction curve and its dynamics settings. speaker.fir was
# Amazon's EQ_50.cfg with a new header, shipped until r293; from r294 the owner
# imports EQ_50.cfg instead. mbcl.conf (ours, lowercase) is not matched.
EQ_*.cfg
MBCL.cfg
speaker.fir
# The Fire OS 5 pair were RENAMED off coefs_*.cfg and so slipped past the
# pattern above and into the tree. Match them by the names they actually had.
biscuit-stock-fbf.cfg
biscuit-stock-filterbank-640.cfg
biscuit-stock-*.cfg

# Owner-imported stock ARTWORK AND AUDIO. Same rule as the configs above and
# the same failure: the patterns there match by extension, and these arrived as
# TARBALLS, so biscuit-earcons.tar.gz (4.3 MB of Amazon earcon recordings) and a
# led-resources bundle full of Fire OS animations were both committed here
# before anyone noticed. Neither is shipped any more - pmOS generates its own
# effects and plays no earcon it did not get from the owner's own device.
#
# biscuit-led-resources.tar.gz is gone too: its last contents, two ordering
# tables, were replaced by biscuit-ring-priorities.json, written from scratch.
# It is matched here so a copy cannot come back.
biscuit-earcons.tar.gz
biscuit-led-resources.tar.gz
*-earcons.tar.gz
*.animation
led-resources/
earcon/

# Captured audio and per-unit data.
*.raw
*.wav
# Except the setup chime, which is ours: generated deterministically by
# tools/make_setup_chime.py, and shipped so the setup page's device check
# can sound before any earcon has been imported.
!device/testing/device-amazon-biscuit/biscuit-setup-chime.wav
# And 50 ms of digital silence (48 kHz stereo, all zeros), which is how "Silent"
# is passed to the voice assistant: it takes each sound as a file path.
!device/testing/device-amazon-biscuit/biscuit-silence.wav
miccal*

# MediaTek WLAN firmware. Owner-imported, not ours to redistribute, and the
# device package's manifest carries only its hash. Kept out by name so a
# careless `git add -A` cannot reintroduce it - which is how it got in.
WIFI_RAM_CODE_8163
WIFI_RAM_CODE
ROMv2_lm_patch_1_0_hdr.bin
ROMv2_lm_patch_1_1_hdr.bin
i2s_to_spi_v34.bin
